 ## Overview
-GSN (Generative Scene Network) decomposes a scene into many independent locally conditioned radiance fields to improve generative performance over global conditioning methods like GRAF [S1]. It distinguishes itself by using modulated linear layers in the generator and a local latent code representation $W \in \mathbb{R}^{c \times s \times s}$, whereas GRAF uses global conditioning with standard linear layers and $\pi$-GAN uses modulated sine layers [S1].
